<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan CPC August profit well off target.</title>
<headline>Taiwan CPC August profit well off target.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp said on Tuesday it posted an August pre-tax profit of T$397 million, well short of a targetted T$1.595 billion.</p>
<p>&quot;Chinese Petroleum failed to meet its planned T$1.595 billion August pre-tax profit,&quot; a company official said. &quot;The main reason was the much higher than expected international oil prices during August.&quot;</p>
<p>The company's oil import costs in August averaged US$18.63 per barrel, higher than a budgeted US$15.62 per barrel, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
